  "description": "The v0.9.0 review-workspace memory_returned receipt vector (design §2/§5, contracts/receipts.md): the fixed seed (32 bytes of 0x01) derives the SAME RFC 8032 keypair as the v0.4.0 vector. Go canonicalizes the memory_returned payload (receipt-payload/v0.10.0 — the authenticated return covers reviewed H1, resulting H2, the REQUIRED correction reason and the complete verified principal snapshot) and the unsigned envelope, hashes them, signs the unsigned envelope with the seed and digests the complete receipt — every computed byte must equal the pinned vector. Node verifies Go's bytes (AC9); Node canonicalizes and signs the same payload and Go verifies it (AC10) — the vector IS the cross-runtime contract. pending_review → returned is NON-terminal: an agent Save on the returned memory creates a NEW revision that re-enters pending_review. Accounting correctness: NOT ASSERTED.",
